<section class="section">
  <div class="container split split--wide-left">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">In 1934, Bethany neighbors came together to organize a fire department. They held the organizational meeting on September 24 in a donated schoolhouse, the Center School.</p>
      <p>The department is still run by volunteers. The Bethany Volunteer Fireman's Association operates it, and the Ambulance Corps is a division of the Association. Today we have three stations, and we meet at Headquarters every Tuesday at 7pm.</p>
      <p>Visitors are welcome on Tuesday. <a href="/join/">Come see us.</a></p>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <h2 class="callout__h">Keeping the past on the road</h2>
      <p>The Association still owns our Muster Truck, a 1950 Ford. See it on the <a href="/about/apparatus/">apparatus page</a>.</p>
      <p>There is also a restored schoolhouse on the Community School campus.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

